# Example gui_script for the perceiver (ehb54/ultrascan-tickets#978).
#
#   us3_somo _pad -I -g examples/perceive.somo
#
# On macOS the throwaway "_pad" first argument is REQUIRED (the arg parser starts at argv[2]);
# on Linux it must be OMITTED. "-I" installs configs silently so nothing blocks on a dialog.
# NOTE: the first run after rebuilding libus_somo only re-installs configs and exits --
# run it twice, the second run actually executes the script.

# Give ABSOLUTE paths below. SOMO changes directory during startup, so a path relative
# to the shell you launched from will not resolve ("ERROR: file does not exist").

# REQUIRED before "perceive build": without the overwrite flag the bead-model write goes
# through setSomoGridFile(), which puts a modal dialog on screen and hangs the headless
# run. Batch mode suppresses those prompts; a gui_script does not, so set it explicitly.
# (Note there is NO such flag for the hydrodynamic calculations -- if your config has
# auto-calculate-hydrodynamics on, a build can still reach a prompt.)
somo overwrite
# and don't launch RasMol windows from a headless run
norasmol
#
# perceiver/data/non-coded/ holds structures that actually contain non-coded residues:
#   2CMD  one citrate, 13 atoms, 3 flagged for review   <- start here
#   3PTB  benzamidine; the only ring-bearing case
#   1MBO  a lone sulfate (its heme and O2 are already coded)
#   5PTI  neutron/deuterated; 50 instances, 18 types -- the stress case
# The demo structures in perceiver/data/ are all fully coded, so (1) finds nothing in them.

# 1. Propose entries for residues somo.residue does NOT code.
#    Without this, SOMO models each such residue as a generic ABB average bead.
perceive /abs/path/to/perceiver/data/non-coded/2CMD.pdb

# 2. Same, but also PUT THE ENTRIES INTO EFFECT: they go into a session overlay of
#    the residue table (<table>.perceived, your own table is untouched), SOMO re-reads
#    it and re-reads the structure. The closing "N residue type(s) still non-coded" is
#    the check -- 0 means the bead builder will use the perceived entries.
perceive apply /abs/path/to/perceiver/data/non-coded/2CMD.pdb

# 3. apply, then BUILD the bead model -- the headless equivalent of the whole GUI
#    session (load, perceive, accept, build). Fails the script if the build fails.
#    Use this, not "apply", to cover anything that only bites at bead-build time:
#    a clean load never reaches the somo.atom lookup.
#    Optional method: somo (default) | somo_o | vdw | grid (a2b). vdw is the sharpest
#    test of a perceived residue -- it relies on atomic hydration, which is proposed.
perceive build /abs/path/to/perceiver/data/non-coded/2CMD.pdb
perceive build somo_o /abs/path/to/perceiver/data/non-coded/2CMD.pdb
perceive build vdw /abs/path/to/perceiver/data/non-coded/2CMD.pdb

# 4. Hand-test: run perception over residues somo.residue DOES code and diff the
#    result against the curated types, using your own installed tables.
perceive compare /abs/path/to/perceiver/data/non-coded/2CMD.pdb

exit
